config IB
	bool "Build the OpenWrt Image Builder"
	depends on !EXTERNAL_TOOLCHAIN || EXTERNAL_TOOLCHAIN_IB
	default BUILDBOT
	help
	  This is essentially a stripped-down version of the buildroot
	  with precompiled packages, kernel image and image building tools.
	  You can use it to generate custom images without compiling anything

config IB_STANDALONE
	bool "Include package repositories"
	default y if !BUILDBOT
	depends on IB
	help
	  Disabling this option will cause the ImageBuilder to embed only
	  toolchain and kmod packages while all other ipk archives will be
	  fetched from online repositories.

config IB_ONLY_SELECTED_DEVICES
	bool "Only build selected devices"
	default n
	depends on IB
	help
	  By default, enabling the Image Builder causes the build system to
	  compile the kernel image of every device of the current
	  target/subtarget and embed it into the Image Builder archive, so
	  that any device profile can later be built from it with
	  'make image PROFILE=...'.

	  Enabling this option restricts the Image Builder to only compile
	  and embed the devices that are actually selected under
	  "Target Devices" in this configuration. This can significantly
	  reduce build time if the Image Builder is only ever going to be
	  used for a known, fixed set of devices.

	  Note: the resulting Image Builder archive will then only be able
	  to build images for the devices selected here, not for the full
	  set of devices of this target/subtarget.
